/*
 * Coding Valley - an interactive C / C++ learning app
 * Written in C with raylib.
 *
 * Features: lessons with syntax-highlighted code, quizzes with explanations,
 * progress tracking saved to progress.dat, mouse + keyboard navigation.
 *
 * Build (Linux):   gcc main.c -o codequest -lraylib -lGL -lm -lpthread -ldl -lrt -lX11
 * Build (macOS):   gcc main.c -o codequest -lraylib -framework OpenGL -framework Cocoa -framework IOKit
 * Build (Windows): gcc main.c -o codequest.exe -lraylib -lopengl32 -lgdi32 -lwinmm
 *
 * Fonts: Liberation Serif (Times New Roman look-alike) + DejaVu Sans Mono are embedded
 *        in this file, so no font files are needed.
 *
 * Campus mode: click "Walk the campus" on the menu to explore as a student. Enter C Hall or
 *   C++ Hall through the door, walk into a classroom and press Space next to a teacher.
 *
 * Shop: earn credits from quizzes, quests and more, then dress your student. Use the pink SHOP building
 *   on campus or the Shop button on the study menu.
 *
 * Menu: sidebar dashboard (Learn path with Khan-style mastery, Practice list of 19 auto-graded coding problems, streak and levels).
 * Lessons have a 'Try this code in the Lab' button (W3Schools style). Practice problems are compiled with gcc/g++ and run against test cases.
 * Mower Farm: a 'The Farmer Was Replaced' style programming game - write C or C++ to drive your student's ride-on mower,
 *   grow crops, buy upgrades (red barn on campus or the Mower Farm button). Windows can be dragged, folded and resized; F11 = fullscreen.
 * Coding Lab: write real C / C++ code, press Run, see the output (needs gcc / g++ installed).
 *   Open it from the study menu or the teal Coding Lab building on campus.
 *
 * Daily Coding Quest: the little gold hut by the path. Face its door and press Space.
 *
 * Quizzes: use the toggle at the top right to switch between multiple choice and typing your answer.
 *
 * Battle Arena: the orange building. Challenge a rival to a head-to-head coding duel.
 *
 * Controls: mouse to click, mouse wheel to scroll, LEFT/RIGHT arrows to change
 *           lesson page, ESC to go back (or quit from the menu).
 */

